She said,
"Things are blowing up.

253
00:12:00,470 --> 00:12:02,847
We've sold out of all
the papers we've had."

254
00:12:02,847 --> 00:12:04,140
That was my first indication

255
00:12:04,140 --> 00:12:06,809
like, wow, people are
really interested in this.

256
00:12:06,809 --> 00:12:08,603
You need to get
a helmet, ma'am!

257
00:12:08,603 --> 00:12:10,021
You need to get a helmet.

258
00:12:10,021 --> 00:12:12,482
It generated
a lot of excitement here.

259
00:12:12,482 --> 00:12:15,193
A lot of businesses had
T-shirts made and sold those,

260
00:12:15,193 --> 00:12:17,904
and the high school kids
had fun with it.

261
00:12:17,904 --> 00:12:19,614
Stephenville
may be typical,

262
00:12:19,614 --> 00:12:21,991
but what's happening
in the skies above it

263
00:12:21,991 --> 00:12:23,785
is a whole 'nother story.

264
00:12:23,785 --> 00:12:26,246
It kind of is the talk
of the town right now.

265
00:12:26,246 --> 00:12:27,872
Angelia Joiner
is a reporter

266
00:12:27,872 --> 00:12:29,332
with the town's newspaper.

267
00:12:29,332 --> 00:12:30,917
She's now on the strangest

268
00:12:30,917 --> 00:12:34,379
and possibly the biggest
story of her life.

269
00:12:34,379 --> 00:12:36,089
It went from
this little story

270
00:12:36,089 --> 00:12:41,761
to this huge, out of control,
worldwide frenzy.

271
00:12:41,761 --> 00:12:44,472
I started getting phone
calls from all over the world:

272
00:12:44,472 --> 00:12:47,058
Brazil, Japan, England.

273
00:12:47,058 --> 00:12:48,309
And the next thing you know,

274
00:12:48,309 --> 00:12:52,021
CNN, and quite a few other
TV things showed up

275
00:12:52,021 --> 00:12:54,440
and wanted our story.

276
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:56,985
What's notable about
the Stephenville case,

277
00:12:56,985 --> 00:12:59,362
and other cases that
are similar to that,

278
00:12:59,362 --> 00:13:01,406
is that despite
the numbers of witnesses

279
00:13:01,406 --> 00:13:04,117
seeing these gigantic craft,

280
00:13:04,117 --> 00:13:07,870
nobody in positions of authority
came to investigate.

281
00:13:07,870 --> 00:13:11,332
That's in contrast to what was
going on in the '40s and '50s

282
00:13:11,332 --> 00:13:12,875
where there was
an Air Force program

283
00:13:12,875 --> 00:13:15,795
and they would
investigate cases.

284
00:13:18,131 --> 00:13:20,967
Here is a picture
that was released just today.

285
00:13:20,967 --> 00:13:23,302
It shows four luminous objects
in formation

286
00:13:23,302 --> 00:13:26,014
in the sky over
Salem, Massachusetts.

287
00:13:26,014 --> 00:13:28,808
Now here on this map
are pinpointed locations

288
00:13:28,808 --> 00:13:31,394
where some 30 saucers
have been sighted

289
00:13:31,394 --> 00:13:34,147
and are still unexplained.

290
00:13:38,318 --> 00:13:42,113
In 1949, the military
started looking into

291
00:13:42,113 --> 00:13:43,906
all these stacks
of UFO reports

292
00:13:43,906 --> 00:13:47,243
that the Air Force
was receiving.

293
00:13:47,243 --> 00:13:49,412
Headquarters United States
Air Force has issued

294
00:13:49,412 --> 00:13:54,584
a directive for a detailed study
of flying disc reports.

295
00:13:54,584 --> 00:13:57,587
The program was initially
called Project Sign,

296
00:13:57,587 --> 00:14:00,423
then became Project Grudge,

297
00:14:00,423 --> 00:14:04,343
and then it was named
Project Blue Book.

298
00:14:05,595 --> 00:14:07,096
Project Blue Book
was operated

299
00:14:07,096 --> 00:14:13,311
out of the dingiest office at
Wright-Patterson Air Force Base.

300
00:14:13,311 --> 00:14:17,523
They had a malfunctioning coffee
pot, they had a couple desks,

301
00:14:17,523 --> 00:14:20,818
they had a big map up
on the wall, and that was it.

302
00:14:20,818 --> 00:14:23,279
But they just had a system down.

303
00:14:23,279 --> 00:14:26,240
Project Blue Book
started as a good faith effort

304
00:14:26,240 --> 00:14:31,746
by the government to collect
reports and investigate UFOs.

305
00:14:31,746 --> 00:14:34,457
When there were big cases, they
would sometimes dispatch someone

306
00:14:34,457 --> 00:14:36,959
to interview the witnesses.

307
00:14:36,959 --> 00:14:38,211
The Air Force
was pretty open

308
00:14:38,211 --> 00:14:39,587
about Project Blue Book.

309
00:14:57,814 --> 00:15:00,316
Alongside
the military employees,

310
00:15:00,316 --> 00:15:01,984
the Air Force felt
that they needed

311
00:15:01,984 --> 00:15:07,865
a credible scientific opinion
to support their research.

312
00:15:07,865 --> 00:15:09,784
Is it in
the realm of possibility

313
00:15:09,784 --> 00:15:14,622
that there are spaceships
someplace in this universe?

314
00:15:14,622 --> 00:15:16,582
Well, if you
put it in the word,

315
00:15:16,582 --> 00:15:19,168
use the word "possibility"
and not "probability,"

316
00:15:19,168 --> 00:15:20,419
then I would have to say,

317
00:15:20,419 --> 00:15:22,880
I think as any scientist
would have to say,

318
00:15:22,880 --> 00:15:26,425
it is certainly possible, yes.

319
00:15:26,425 --> 00:15:30,179
J. Allen Hynek was a
mild-mannered college professor

320
00:15:30,179 --> 00:15:32,306
from Ohio State University.

321
00:15:32,306 --> 00:15:35,560
His job was to go through
all these stacks of UFO reports

322
00:15:35,560 --> 00:15:37,353
that the Air Force was receiving

323
00:15:37,353 --> 00:15:40,648
and try to find out
what's going on.

324
00:15:40,648 --> 00:15:42,441
Project Blue Book examined

325
00:15:42,441 --> 00:15:46,112
over 12,000 UFO sightings,

326
00:15:46,112 --> 00:15:48,239
many of them bore
a striking resemblance

327
00:15:48,239 --> 00:15:50,741
to what we're seeing today.

328
00:15:50,741 --> 00:15:54,745
Crafts with a similar shape,
sometimes the same color,

329
00:15:54,745 --> 00:15:57,665
hovering, then shooting off
instantaneously

330
00:15:57,665 --> 00:15:59,584
at hypersonic speeds.

331
00:15:59,584 --> 00:16:03,546
Multiple, multiple cases
like that.

332
00:16:03,546 --> 00:16:05,715
While working
for Project Blue Book,

333
00:16:05,715 --> 00:16:09,635
Hynek noticed that he was able
to explain 80% of cases.

334
00:16:09,635 --> 00:16:14,432
But he also noticed that there
was about a 20% residue of cases

335
00:16:14,432 --> 00:16:17,310
that he hadn't been able
to explain away.

336
00:16:17,310 --> 00:16:20,188
Allen Hynek
came into the UFO project

337
00:16:20,188 --> 00:16:23,566
with the attitude which is,
there's nothing to UFOs,

338
00:16:23,566 --> 00:16:26,194
but he was a good enough
scientist to say,

339
00:16:26,194 --> 00:16:27,695
"Wait a minute,

340
00:16:27,695 --> 00:16:31,240
I'm seeing reports here that
are not easily explainable."

341
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:34,202
The Air Force
and their UFO study project

342
00:16:34,202 --> 00:16:36,621
may have been making
an honest effort

343
00:16:36,621 --> 00:16:39,457
to clear the air
about the phenomenon.

344
00:16:39,457 --> 00:16:41,876
Unfortunately,
it didn't last too long,

345
00:16:41,876 --> 00:16:45,379
simply because they were just
overwhelmed with reports.

346
00:17:03,481 --> 00:17:04,982
This is the Kremlin.

347
00:17:04,982 --> 00:17:08,653
Russia today is regarded as
a grave threat to our nation,

348
00:17:08,653 --> 00:17:11,739
to our freedom,
to the peace of the world.

349
00:17:16,077 --> 00:17:17,495
In the '40s and '50s,

350
00:17:17,495 --> 00:17:20,665
tensions with Russia
were building.

351
00:17:20,665 --> 00:17:22,833
The Cold War was
so intense at that point,

352
00:17:22,833 --> 00:17:25,086
so there was a genuine concern

353
00:17:25,086 --> 00:17:28,881
that the UFO phenomenon
could be exploited.

354
00:17:28,881 --> 00:17:30,758
The US government
felt adversaries

355
00:17:30,758 --> 00:17:32,843
could hoax UFO sightings

356
00:17:32,843 --> 00:17:35,596
and then clog up
our reporting channels

357
00:17:35,596 --> 00:17:37,515
and then have a surprise attack.

358
00:17:37,515 --> 00:17:39,684
So the idea was that
the UFO problem

359
00:17:39,684 --> 00:17:41,686
was not a security problem
as such,

360
00:17:41,686 --> 00:17:44,564
meaning aliens aren't going
to land and, and attack us.

361
00:17:44,564 --> 00:17:48,025
What the UFO problem was,
it was a sociological problem,

362
00:17:48,025 --> 00:17:52,780
and it was one that demanded
a different approach.

363
00:17:52,780 --> 00:17:54,824
The CIA entered the picture

364
00:17:54,824 --> 00:17:57,118
by convening a panel
of top scientists

365
00:17:57,118 --> 00:17:59,036
to examine UFO phenomenon.

366
00:17:59,036 --> 00:18:03,291
The thinking was that the enemy
could exploit UFOs as a decoy

367
00:18:03,291 --> 00:18:06,419
in the preparation for
an attack on the United States.

368
00:18:06,419 --> 00:18:08,045
Five outstanding scientists

369
00:18:08,045 --> 00:18:11,340
and various Air Force and CIA
representatives were to meet.

370
00:18:11,340 --> 00:18:15,636
Among the panel members
was J. Allen Hynek.

371
00:18:15,636 --> 00:18:19,598
In 1953,
the Central Intelligence Agency

372
00:18:19,598 --> 00:18:24,186
formed a scientific panel led
by a highly regarded scientist

373
00:18:24,186 --> 00:18:28,274
named Robertson to examine this
phenomenon and its implications.

374
00:18:28,274 --> 00:18:32,194
The Robertson Panel was a
group of hand-picked scientists

375
00:18:32,194 --> 00:18:35,156
who came together to try
to determine a way

376
00:18:35,156 --> 00:18:38,993
to damp down
public interest in UFOs.

377
00:18:38,993 --> 00:18:40,536
Dr. Hynek was
actually brought in

378
00:18:40,536 --> 00:18:44,832
to be a consulting witness
to the Robertson Panel.

379
00:18:44,832 --> 00:18:48,544
The panel members
were seated around this table.

380
00:18:48,544 --> 00:18:52,465
It was a rather somber and
impressive occasion, actually.

381
00:18:52,465 --> 00:18:55,176
The mission given
by the Robertson Panel

382
00:18:55,176 --> 00:19:01,807
was essentially to make people
stop filing UFO reports.

383
00:19:01,807 --> 00:19:05,770
They proposed two methods
to damp down public enthusiasm.

384
00:19:05,770 --> 00:19:08,522
One was through debunking.

385
00:19:08,522 --> 00:19:10,983
The second one
was through education,

386
00:19:10,983 --> 00:19:12,860
teaching people to explain UFOs

387
00:19:12,860 --> 00:19:16,489
in other ways than
something extraordinary.

388
00:19:16,489 --> 00:19:20,451
It was an extremely important
moment in the evolution

389
00:19:20,451 --> 00:19:24,497
of how government was going
to engage with this topic.

390
00:19:24,497 --> 00:19:28,250
This became the launch of taboo
on a more official level,

391
00:19:28,250 --> 00:19:32,088
where it was becoming
policy in a way.

392
00:19:32,088 --> 00:19:35,341
Ridicule became sanctioned.

393
00:19:35,341 --> 00:19:38,969
The Robertson Panel conclusion
seemed to have a big impact

394
00:19:38,969 --> 00:19:40,680
on Project Blue Book.

395
00:19:40,680 --> 00:19:44,016
The project began to dismiss
as many cases as possible

396
00:19:44,016 --> 00:19:47,770
and provide sometimes
ridiculous explanations for them

397
00:19:47,770 --> 00:19:51,649
just to have an answer
and make them go away.

398
00:19:51,649 --> 00:19:53,526
Hynek's job
became going through

399
00:19:53,526 --> 00:19:55,069
all these UFO reports

400
00:19:55,069 --> 00:19:57,988
and explain them away
as natural occurrences.

401
00:19:57,988 --> 00:20:02,785
Comet, meteor, shooting star,
sun dog, eclipse.

402
00:20:02,785 --> 00:20:06,831
I would say the great
majority are balloons, meteors,

403
00:20:06,831 --> 00:20:10,835
satellites, aircraft seen with
the sun glinting off of them.

404
00:20:10,835 --> 00:20:15,214
Generally, quite usual things
seen under unusual circumstances

405
00:20:15,214 --> 00:20:17,133
or surprising circumstances.

406
00:20:17,133 --> 00:20:19,802
Dr. Hynek did his job
very thoroughly.

407
00:20:19,802 --> 00:20:23,347
Allen was a fellow trying
to please the Air Force

408
00:20:23,347 --> 00:20:26,058
and what they wanted.

409
00:20:26,058 --> 00:20:27,768
Hynek would have
a bunch of reports

410
00:20:27,768 --> 00:20:29,061
dropped on his desk,

411
00:20:29,061 --> 00:20:31,939
and he would explain
them all away.

412
00:20:31,939 --> 00:20:35,651
If a report said
"probable airliner,"

413
00:20:35,651 --> 00:20:38,571
they would cross out "probable"
and just say "airliner,"

414
00:20:38,571 --> 00:20:40,030
and that's what the witness saw.

415
00:20:40,030 --> 00:20:43,993
It was kind of an insult to the,
to the, to the intelligence

416
00:20:43,993 --> 00:20:46,162
of the American people.

417
00:20:46,162 --> 00:20:48,706
Hynek had taken the job
for the extra money.

418
00:20:48,706 --> 00:20:52,042
Struggling young professional
with a growing family,

419
00:20:52,042 --> 00:20:54,253
of course he's not gonna
turn down work.

420
00:20:54,253 --> 00:20:55,796
But behind the scenes,

421
00:20:55,796 --> 00:21:00,551
Hynek gradually realized that
this was a scientific problem.

422
00:21:00,551 --> 00:21:04,263
But he wouldn't go out
and state it publicly.

423
00:21:04,263 --> 00:21:07,475
He didn't want to do that,
because it would have been

424
00:21:07,475 --> 00:21:11,562
what the Air Force
didn't want him to do.

425
00:21:11,562 --> 00:21:13,731
Even though
it took place in 1953,

426
00:21:13,731 --> 00:21:15,774
the Robertson Panel
was so potent

427
00:21:15,774 --> 00:21:19,153
in terms of its desire
to clamp down, to ridicule,

428
00:21:19,153 --> 00:21:20,738
to debunk, and to, quote,

429
00:21:20,738 --> 00:21:24,241
"educate people to interpret
UFOs in other ways,"

430
00:21:24,241 --> 00:21:26,535
its legacy carried on
through the decades,

431
00:21:26,535 --> 00:21:29,079
and it impacted cases
like Stephenville

432
00:21:29,079 --> 00:21:31,874
and other cases of the time.

433
00:21:33,375 --> 00:21:35,085
Alright, stand by!

434
00:21:36,754 --> 00:21:39,632
Last week, several people
in Stephenville, Texas,

435
00:21:39,632 --> 00:21:41,926
a small, rural town
of about 15,000,

436
00:21:41,926 --> 00:21:44,762
witnessed what many
are calling a UFO.

437
00:21:44,762 --> 00:21:46,680
In Selden, Texas,
is Steve Allen.

438
00:21:46,680 --> 00:21:48,891
Also there is Angelia Joiner,

439
00:21:48,891 --> 00:21:50,726
staff writer for
the Empire-Tribune,

440
00:21:50,726 --> 00:21:52,728
the local newspaper
in Stephenville.

441
00:21:52,728 --> 00:21:55,606
Angelia, what are some witnesses
telling you?

442
00:21:55,606 --> 00:21:57,608
The thing that I hear
over and over and over

443
00:21:57,608 --> 00:21:59,527
is how bright the lights were,

444
00:21:59,527 --> 00:22:05,491
so I think there's been a lot
of consistency in the spottings.

445
00:22:05,491 --> 00:22:08,577
It was Angelia
that started digging deep.

446
00:22:08,577 --> 00:22:11,705
She was hell-bent on trying
to find out what we saw

447
00:22:11,705 --> 00:22:13,666
and what happened.

448
00:22:13,666 --> 00:22:17,836
And it almost consumed her.

449
00:22:17,836 --> 00:22:21,048
The incredible thing
about the Stephenville sightings

450
00:22:21,048 --> 00:22:25,094
was that witnesses reported
seeing F-16 fighters

451
00:22:25,094 --> 00:22:27,054
pursuing this object.

452
00:22:27,054 --> 00:22:29,306
I heard this
really, really loud noise.

453
00:22:29,306 --> 00:22:31,350
And I ran out the front door,

454
00:22:31,350 --> 00:22:34,436
and there were fighter jets
chasing those lights.

455
00:22:34,436 --> 00:22:37,189
Angelia wanted to know
what the Air Force knew

456
00:22:37,189 --> 00:22:39,942
about the two F-16s
and what we saw.

457
00:22:39,942 --> 00:22:44,113
She got in touch with the naval
air station in Fort Worth

458
00:22:44,113 --> 00:22:47,241
and talked to
a Major Karl Lewis.

459
00:22:47,241 --> 00:22:49,785
And Major Karl Lewis said
we didn't have any aircraft

460
00:22:49,785 --> 00:22:52,663
in your area at that time.

461
00:22:55,374 --> 00:22:57,376
I feel like we wasn't
given the truth,

462
00:22:57,376 --> 00:22:59,920
and the military didn't seem
like they was interested

463
00:22:59,920 --> 00:23:02,172
in any questions.

464
00:23:02,172 --> 00:23:03,966
Then on about the tenth day,

465
00:23:03,966 --> 00:23:08,095
the military issued
a press release.

466
00:23:08,095 --> 00:23:10,514
Now in a plot line
that's out of The X-Files,

467
00:23:10,514 --> 00:23:14,018
Air Force officials are saying
they concede they had F-16s

468
00:23:14,018 --> 00:23:18,355
over Stephenville, Texas,
on the evening of January 8th.

469
00:23:18,355 --> 00:23:19,940
Major Karl Lewis says there was

470
00:23:19,940 --> 00:23:22,151
an internal
communications mistake.

471
00:23:30,326 --> 00:23:33,329
The plot thickened,
but the Air Force wouldn't say

472
00:23:33,329 --> 00:23:39,001
why they did in fact
have F-16s in the area.

473
00:23:39,001 --> 00:23:41,629
Angelia Joiner says
that the Air Force's admission

474
00:23:41,629 --> 00:23:43,797
that it did indeed
have fighter jets,

475
00:23:43,797 --> 00:23:47,843
as reported by the witnesses,
bolsters their story all around.

476
00:23:47,843 --> 00:23:49,553
Military coming out
with this at this point

477
00:23:49,553 --> 00:23:51,805
just is going to
fuel the fire for,

478
00:23:51,805 --> 00:23:55,851
okay, there is something
going on, now what is it?

479
00:23:57,770 --> 00:24:00,773
We thought their attempt
to try to explain it away

480
00:24:00,773 --> 00:24:03,442
was terribly strange.

481
00:24:03,442 --> 00:24:06,028
We had more questions
than answers.

482
00:24:10,324 --> 00:24:13,410
UFO reports,
hoax or serious sightings,

483
00:24:13,410 --> 00:24:17,289
wind up here at Wright-Patterson
air field in Dayton, Ohio.

484
00:24:17,289 --> 00:24:21,293
The Air Force investigative unit
is known as Project Blue Book.

485
00:24:21,293 --> 00:24:23,545
In the wake of
the Robertson Panel,

486
00:24:23,545 --> 00:24:25,589
Project Blue Book
was investigating

487
00:24:25,589 --> 00:24:27,007
these civilian reports

488
00:24:27,007 --> 00:24:30,052
as a way to tamp down
public concern.

489
00:24:30,052 --> 00:24:32,513
For example, in Michigan,
there were at one point

490
00:24:32,513 --> 00:24:36,392
a large number of sightings
by people in a community there.

491
00:24:36,392 --> 00:24:41,522
And Walter Cronkite, the arbiter
of truth for many Americans,

492
00:24:41,522 --> 00:24:42,982
covered the story.

493
00:24:42,982 --> 00:24:45,567
The great
flying saucer mystery of 1966

494
00:24:45,567 --> 00:24:49,780
began here, near
Dexter, Michigan, late in March.

495
00:24:49,780 --> 00:24:52,241
As I turned around
to come back on the porch,

496
00:24:52,241 --> 00:24:58,122
I looked to the north of me,
and looked like a falling star,

497
00:24:58,122 --> 00:25:01,041
meteor, it was red
and kind of coming down.

498
00:25:01,041 --> 00:25:03,585
Frank Mannor's UFO
remained over his swamp

499
00:25:03,585 --> 00:25:05,671
more than four hours.

500
00:25:05,671 --> 00:25:10,134
